  "id": "COMPOUND:20099 - PROTEIN:5783",
  "verbalization": "The compound (1S,3E,4S,5S,6S)-4,5-dihydroxy-3-(3-methylbut-2-enylidene)-7-oxabicyclo[4.1.0]heptan-2-one is linked to M19-MEL through a series of target relationships. It is directly targeted by Thioredoxin, mitochondrial, which in turn is targeted by Rhetsinine and Flavipin. These intermediates suggest a pathway where the compound may act as a regulator of Thioredoxin activity, potentially influencing downstream metabolic processes. The evidence points to a possible role in modulating mitochondrial function, as Thioredoxin is involved in redox regulation and cellular stress responses. The connection to M19-MEL, a protein involved in sialylation and cellular signaling, implies a broader impact on cellular metabolism and signaling pathways. The integration of these relationships highlights a potential mechanism where the compound influences mitochondrial function, which in turn affects M19-MEL activity, suggesting a role in cellular homeostasis.",
